course: dictionary
lesson: 9002
title: Sketchy: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «My memory of the trip is sketchy» means you only remember the main parts, not the details. Here sketchy means not complete or detailed.
explain: A sketchy drawing has quick, rough lines, because it was done fast, like a sketch. A sketchy answer gives only the main points. Ask yourself: is the sentence about drawing, detail or safety? The words around it will show you.
explain: Young people also use sketchy as slang. «That link looks sketchy» means it seems shady or unsafe. In «Lily's mum checks that sketchy_scot is a real girl in Inverness», sketchy_scot is a username, and the check is a safety clue: you need to know who you are talking to before you trust them.
fact: Sketchy has three main meanings: not complete or detailed; drawn quickly and roughly; and, as slang, dodgy or unsafe.
fact: «Sketchy notes» lack detail, and «my memory is sketchy» means you don't remember well.
fact: «That's sketchy» means it feels shady or unsafe.
fact: A sketchy link or website should not be clicked.
fact: Sketchy changes in comparisons: sketchier, sketchiest.
exercise: «The teacher wrote sketchy notes on the board.» What does sketchy mean here? | Brightly coloured | *Not complete or detailed | Very old | Sung loudly
exercise: «Ben found a sketchy link in an email.» What should Ben do with it? | Print it and keep it | Forward it to all his friends | Click it quickly to see what it is | *Do not click it, and tell a grown-up
exercise: «The artist's sketchy drawing used quick, loose lines.» What does sketchy mean? | Finished in perfect detail | *Drawn quickly and roughly | Very dangerous | Made of wood
test: «My memory of the holiday is sketchy.» What does sketchy suggest? | I forgot my camera | I went on holiday twice | *I don't remember it well | I remember every single detail
test: «That website looks sketchy, so Maya closed it.» Why did Maya close it? | It loaded too slowly | *It seemed dodgy or unsafe | It had too many pictures | It was too bright
exam: «The plan was sketchy, with no times or places.» What does sketchy mean? | *Not complete or detailed | Dangerous to climb | Very old | Drawn with bright paint
